<p>Activity 2 demonstrates least-squares regression with technology. Put students in groups so that they can help each other with the keystrokes. It is probably not a good idea to require students to memorize the steps in this process; allow them to use a copy of the instructions when they use technology for regression.</p> 

<p>The scatterplots in Example 3 (literacy and birth rate) and Homework Problem 3 (Miss America BMI's) are more complex; students should not be required to find regression equations for data sets of this size. However, they should be asked to read and interpret information from the graph.</p>


